  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Deleting a group that has any amount of members who aren't yourself (regardless of browser) will return a 403 \"ERR_BAD_REQUEST\" and do nothing.\n\nI'm not really sure why this was designed in this way, since you as an admin could just individually kick/ban all members first and close off the group *before* deleting it. Adding a bunch of steps to the process certainly makes deleting large groups form existance harder and a more definitive task, but this could be just communicated clearer through the normal deletion process. (Perhaps in the future, attempts to delete a groups containing members will prompt for a paragraph explaining *why* and submit it to support to make the final decision.)",
